@article{kato-ogawa-1983,
  author  = {Kato, Mitsuhiro and Ogawa, Kaku},
  title   = {Covariant quantization of string based on {BRS} invariance},
  journal = {Nuclear Physics B},
  volume  = {212},
  pages   = {443--460},
  year    = {1983},
  doi     = {10.1016/0550-3213(83)90680-6},
  note    = {元数据已核实（INSPIRE 记录 177600；卷页由 FGZ 1986 参考文献 5 独立佐证）。报告号 **KUNS 637**（INSPIRE report_numbers，L2；检索后端 L4 对此有异议，认为 637 属 RIFP 系列且 Kato 当时在东京——两方冲突未裁决，此处按 INSPIRE 记）。
             **摘要已升级为逐字（INSPIRE，2026-09-10）**：「Covariant canonical quantization of the bosonic string is performed, based on the BRS invariance principle. Defining a physical state by a modified form of Kugo-Ojima's subsidiary condition Q_B |phys> = 0 ( Q_B = BRS charge), we prove a no-ghost theorem in a simple manner. There an interesting relation between critical dimension and BRS symmetry is noticed; namely, the conditions D = 26 and alpha_0 = 1 for the space-time dimension D and the zero-intercept alpha_0 of leading trajectory are required by the nilpotency Q_B^2 = 0 of the BRS charge. In addition, ghost number fractionization is observed in this system.」
             **方向已定：给的是「Q_B^2 = 0 ==> (D = 26 且 a = 1)」（required by），摘要中没有反方向，因此没有「当且仅当」。**
             仍未核实：是否已写成 Ker Q_B / Im Q_B = OCQ 物理态 的同构形式；定理编号。正文未获取（ScienceDirect 403；未找到 KEK/京大扫描件）。见 extractions/brst-cohomology-sources.md §6 与 primary-sources-round2.md §6。}
}

